---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="What is TF-CBT?" description="A parent-friendly guide to Trauma-Focused Cognitive Behavioral Therapy - what it is, how it works, and how to support your child.">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 sm:py-16">
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="text-sm mb-6">
      <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-forest-400">
        <li><a href="/families" class="hover:text-bronze-500 transition-colors">For Families</a></li>
        <li>/</li>
        <li class="text-forest-100">TF-CBT</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header with visual emphasis -->
    <header class="mb-10">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <div class="w-16 h-16 bg-bronze-500 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center text-white flex-shrink-0">
          <svg class="w-8 h-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M9.663 17h4.673M12 3v1m6.364 1.636l-.707.707M21 12h-1M4 12H3m3.343-5.657l-.707-.707m2.828 9.9a5 5 0 117.072 0l-.548.547A3.374 3.374 0 0014 18.469V19a2 2 0 11-4 0v-.531c0-.895-.356-1.754-.988-2.386l-.548-.547z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-bronze-500 font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-wide">Understanding Your Child's Treatment</p>
          <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold text-bronze-gradient">
            What is TF-CBT?
          </h1>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Key points as horizontal pills -->
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-10">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 bg-forest-700 text-bronze-400 rounded-full text-sm">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
        </svg>
        Evidence-based
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 bg-forest-700 text-bronze-400 rounded-full text-sm">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
        </svg>
        Parents are partners
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 bg-forest-700 text-bronze-400 rounded-full text-sm">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
        </svg>
        Builds coping skills
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 bg-forest-700 text-bronze-400 rounded-full text-sm">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
        </svg>
        Structured approach
      </span>
    </div>

    <!-- Two column layout for main content -->
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">

      <!-- Left column: Main content cards -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-6">

        <!-- Understanding TF-CBT Card -->
        <div class="bg-forest-800 rounded-xl border border-forest-600 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-forest-600 to-forest-700 px-5 py-3">
            <h2 class="text-white font-semibold flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
              </svg>
              Understanding TF-CBT
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 space-y-4">
            <p class="text-forest-200 leading-relaxed">
              TF-CBT stands for <strong>Trauma-Focused Cognitive Behavioral Therapy</strong>. It's a structured therapy designed specifically for children and teens who have experienced trauma.
            </p>
            <p class="text-forest-200 leading-relaxed">
              Unlike some therapies where only the child attends, TF-CBT involves <strong>you as a partner in your child's healing</strong>. You'll learn the same skills your child is learning so you can support them at home.
            </p>
            <p class="text-forest-200 leading-relaxed">
              The therapy helps children understand their feelings about what happened, develop healthy coping skills, and process their trauma in a safe, gradual way.
            </p>
            <div class="p-4 bg-forest-700 border-l-4 border-forest-500 rounded-r-lg">
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-forest-100 mb-1">Strong Research Support</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-forest-200">TF-CBT has been studied extensively and is one of the most effective treatments for childhood trauma and PTSD. It works for many types of trauma.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- The PRACTICE Model Card -->
        <div class="bg-forest-800 rounded-xl border border-forest-600 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-bronze-600 to-bronze-700 px-5 py-3">
            <h2 class="text-white font-semibold flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2m-3 7h3m-3 4h3m-6-4h.01M9 16h.01" />
              </svg>
              The PRACTICE Model
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5">
            <p class="text-forest-200 mb-6">
              TF-CBT follows a structured approach called <strong>PRACTICE</strong>. Each letter stands for a component of treatment. Your child's therapist will explain each part in detail as you go.
            </p>

            <div class="space-y-4">
              <!-- P -->
              <div class="bg-forest-700/50 rounded-lg p-4 border-l-4 border-forest-400">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-forest-500 text-white rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">P</span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-forest-100">Psychoeducation</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-forest-300 mt-1">Learning about trauma and how it affects the brain and body. Both you and your child receive this education.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- R -->
              <div class="bg-forest-700 rounded-lg p-4 border-l-4 border-forest-500">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-bronze-500 text-white rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">R</span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-forest-100">Relaxation</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-forest-300 mt-1">Learning calming techniques like breathing exercises and muscle relaxation to manage stress and anxiety.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- A -->
              <div class="bg-forest-700 rounded-lg p-4 border-l-4 border-bronze-500">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-forest-400 text-white rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">A</span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-forest-100">Affective Modulation</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-forest-300 mt-1">Identifying and managing big feelings. Building a vocabulary for emotions and learning healthy ways to express them.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- C -->
              <div class="bg-forest-700 rounded-lg p-4 border-l-4 border-bronze-400">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-bronze-400 text-white rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">C</span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-forest-100">Cognitive Coping</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-forest-300 mt-1">Understanding how thoughts, feelings, and behaviors connect. Learning to notice unhelpful thinking patterns.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- T -->
              <div class="bg-forest-700/50 rounded-lg p-4 border-l-4 border-forest-500">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-forest-500 text-white rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">T</span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-forest-100">Trauma Narrative</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-forest-300 mt-1">Gradually telling their trauma story in a safe, supported way. This happens only when your child is ready and has the coping skills they need.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- I -->
              <div class="bg-forest-700/50 rounded-lg p-4 border-l-4 border-forest-400">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-forest-400 text-white rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">I</span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-forest-100">In Vivo Mastery <span class="font-normal text-forest-300 text-sm">(real-life practice)</span></h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-forest-300 mt-1">Facing trauma reminders in real life, step by step. Used when avoidance is getting in the way of everyday activities.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- C -->
              <div class="bg-forest-700 rounded-lg p-4 border-l-4 border-bronze-500">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-bronze-500 text-white rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">C</span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-forest-100">Conjoint Sessions</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-forest-300 mt-1">Parent and child come together to share the trauma narrative and strengthen your connection. This is a powerful healing experience for families.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- E -->
              <div class="bg-forest-700 rounded-lg p-4 border-l-4 border-forest-500">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-forest-500 text-white rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">E</span>
                  <div>
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-forest-100">Enhancing Safety</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-forest-300 mt-1">Building safety skills and planning for the future. Helping your child feel prepared and confident going forward.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Your Role as a Parent Card -->
        <div class="bg-forest-800 rounded-xl border border-forest-600 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-forest-600 to-forest-700 px-5 py-3">
            <h2 class="text-white font-semibold flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" />
              </svg>
              Your Role as a Parent
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 space-y-4">
            <p class="text-forest-200 leading-relaxed">
              In TF-CBT, you're not just dropping your child off — you're an active participant in their healing.
            </p>
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-bronze-400 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                </svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-forest-200"><strong>You'll have your own sessions</strong> with the therapist to learn each skill before your child does</p>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-bronze-400 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                </svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-forest-200"><strong>You'll practice skills at home</strong> together between sessions</p>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-bronze-400 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                </svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-forest-200"><strong>You'll join conjoint sessions</strong> where you and your child share their trauma narrative together</p>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-bronze-400 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                </svg>
                <p class="text-sm text-forest-200"><strong>The therapist will guide you</strong> on how to respond supportively to your child's disclosures</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 bg-forest-700/50 border-l-4 border-forest-400 rounded-r-lg">
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-forest-100 mb-1">Parents Make a Difference</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-forest-200">Research shows that parental involvement is one of the key factors that makes TF-CBT so effective. Your support matters.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Questions Card -->
        <div class="bg-forest-800 rounded-xl border border-forest-600 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-bronze-600 to-bronze-700 px-5 py-3">
            <h2 class="text-white font-semibold flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8.228 9c.549-1.165 2.03-2 3.772-2 2.21 0 4 1.343 4 3 0 1.4-1.278 2.575-3.006 2.907-.542.104-.994.54-.994 1.093m0 3h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
              </svg>
              Common Questions
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 space-y-4">
            <details class="group border border-forest-600 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-3 bg-forest-700 cursor-pointer hover:bg-forest-700 transition-colors">
                <span class="font-medium text-forest-100 text-sm">How long does TF-CBT take?</span>
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-forest-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="p-4 bg-forest-800 border-t border-forest-600">
                <p class="text-sm text-forest-200">TF-CBT is typically 12-25 sessions, though this varies based on your child's needs. Some children may need more time to build skills before working on the trauma narrative.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="group border border-forest-600 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-3 bg-forest-700 cursor-pointer hover:bg-forest-700 transition-colors">
                <span class="font-medium text-forest-100 text-sm">Will my child have to talk about what happened?</span>
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-forest-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="p-4 bg-forest-800 border-t border-forest-600">
                <p class="text-sm text-forest-200">Yes, but only when they're ready. Your child will first learn coping skills, then gradually work up to telling their story. The therapist ensures they feel safe and in control throughout the process.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="group border border-forest-600 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-3 bg-forest-700 cursor-pointer hover:bg-forest-700 transition-colors">
                <span class="font-medium text-forest-100 text-sm">What age is TF-CBT for?</span>
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-forest-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="p-4 bg-forest-800 border-t border-forest-600">
                <p class="text-sm text-forest-200">TF-CBT is designed for children and teens ages 3-18. The therapist adapts the activities and language to be appropriate for your child's developmental level.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="group border border-forest-600 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-3 bg-forest-700 cursor-pointer hover:bg-forest-700 transition-colors">
                <span class="font-medium text-forest-100 text-sm">What types of trauma does TF-CBT treat?</span>
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-forest-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="p-4 bg-forest-800 border-t border-forest-600">
                <p class="text-sm text-forest-200">TF-CBT can help with many types of trauma including abuse, witnessing violence, accidents, loss of a loved one, natural disasters, and medical trauma.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right column: Sticky Sidebar -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-1">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 space-y-6">
          <!-- How to Support Your Child -->
          <div class="bg-forest-800 rounded-xl border border-forest-600 overflow-hidden">
            <div class="bg-bronze-500 px-4 py-3">
              <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4.318 6.318a4.5 4.5 0 000 6.364L12 20.364l7.682-7.682a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364-6.364L12 7.636l-1.318-1.318a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364 0z" />
                </svg>
                How to Support Your Child
              </h2>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 space-y-4">
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-forest-400 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">During Treatment</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm text-forest-200">
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-bronze-400 mt-0.5">•</span>
                    Attend your parent sessions
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-bronze-400 mt-0.5">•</span>
                    Practice skills together at home
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-bronze-400 mt-0.5">•</span>
                    Praise their effort and courage
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-forest-400 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">When They Share</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm text-forest-200">
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-bronze-400 mt-0.5">•</span>
                    Listen calmly without interrupting
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-bronze-400 mt-0.5">•</span>
                    Validate their feelings
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-bronze-400 mt-0.5">•</span>
                    Thank them for trusting you
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-forest-400 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">At Home</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm text-forest-200">
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-bronze-400 mt-0.5">•</span>
                    Keep consistent routines
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-bronze-400 mt-0.5">•</span>
                    Use relaxation techniques together
                  </li>
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="text-bronze-400 mt-0.5">•</span>
                    Be patient — progress isn't linear
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- For Caregivers Note -->
          <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-forest-700 to-forest-700/50 rounded-xl border border-forest-500 overflow-hidden">
            <div class="px-4 py-3 border-b border-forest-500">
              <h2 class="font-semibold text-forest-100 text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4.318 6.318a4.5 4.5 0 000 6.364L12 20.364l7.682-7.682a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364-6.364L12 7.636l-1.318-1.318a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364 0z" />
                </svg>
                For Caregivers
              </h2>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4">
              <p class="text-sm text-forest-200 leading-relaxed">
                Hearing about your child's trauma can bring up difficult feelings of your own. This is normal. Talk to the therapist about getting support for yourself — taking care of you helps you take care of them.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Back Link -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-forest-600">
      <a href="/families" class="text-bronze-500 hover:text-bronze-400 transition-colors flex items-center gap-2">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Family Resources
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
